        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 4:33PM MDT by NWS Denver CO</headline>
        <description>At 433 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 7
miles southeast of Aurora, or 18 miles east of Denver, moving east at
15 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Eastern Aurora, Watkins and Manila Village.
</description>
        <instruction>Monitor the weather situation closely and be alert for threatening
weather conditions.</instruction>
